/cover.out

# Compiled binaries. `go build` in the repo root leaves one named after the
# module or after whatever -o was passed; three of them were committed before
# this line existed, at ~97 MB each. A pattern per name is not the answer --
# the next one will have a new name -- so the binaries the build actually
# produces are listed, and `git add -A` no longer sweeps them in.
/reader
/newsreader
/reader-fixed
# …and it happened again: `go build ./cmd/dmg` leaves /dmg, which `git add -A`
# swept into a commit at 4 MB. The names are listed because that is what this
# file can do; the actual remedy is `go build -o /tmp/...` from the start.
/dmg
/bundle
/*.png
.DS_Store

# Coverage profiles: produced by `go test -coverprofile`, never committed.
cov.out
*.cov
coverage.out
app.test
